{"id":"20260825T184811.768898711Z-f4da7af2","time":"2026-08-25T18:48:11.768898711Z","session_id":"session-20260825T184540.175822448Z","task_id":"task-1787683540176126019","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  A task interrupted after its plan was authorised cannot be resumed: nothing reconstructs, from the recorded event stream, which tasks were left in that state.\n\nAdd to internal/session the exported type and function:\n\n    type Interrupted struct { TaskID, Task, Plan, Review string }\n    func FindInterrupted(events []event.Event) []Interrupted\n\nGiven a session's events it returns one entry per task that was created, had its authority RESOLVED, and never reached a terminal workflow outcome -- carrying the task text, the plan, and the reviewer's latest status if one exists. A plan that was merely PROPOSED is not resumable: a task still waiting on a human has produced no work to continue. Tasks that completed or failed are excluded, entries come back in the order the tasks first appeared, and a task with no recorded request text is not returned.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei classified this exact file scope as ARCHITECTURE_SENSITIVE with current authoritative evidence and sufficient coverage. (internal/session/store.go and internal/session/interrupted_test.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Only an explicit authority resolution may satisfy the boundary, and a task still awaiting approval must never be resumed. (FindInterrupted eligibility) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] event.Event records TaskID, Source, Kind, Summary, and Payload, with TaskCreated, PlanProposed, AuthorityResolved, WorkflowCompleted, WorkflowFailed, and Status kinds. (internal/event/event.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The workflow stores request text in TaskCreated.Summary, the bounded plan in PlanProposed.Payload, authority answers as AuthorityResolved events, and reviewer decisions as reviewer-sourced Status events. (internal/workflow/engine.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] FindInterrupted is not present in the current checkout. (internal/session) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The task-aware briefing retry returned exactly: tool call error: tool call failed for `sensei/task_briefing`\n\nCaused by:\n    Mcp error: -32000: no task session exists in this repository (task-aware admission context) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  UNACCEPTABLE — none established: the plan states it will act outside the worktree\n    effect: the plan declares an outward action: production\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: human-authority-required\n"}
